              <MultilingualTextItem ID="21" CompositionName="Items">
                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text> The block compares the values of the inputs _in1 ... in8_ with the value of the input _compareValue_ and generates a collective OR signal from these comparisons. If at least one of the values of in1 ... in8 is equal with _compareValue_, the value of _compareValue_ is written to output “value”.  
Otherwise, “value” is written with the value 0.  
Use Case example: With this, a "summary signal" can be formed, e.g. for production data "Limit Values", with which a button can be animated (Button "ProdData", "LimitValues"). 

**Block call example**  

The call is shown as “Ladder Diagram” (LAD), without parameters.  

**Calling interface**  

The block is called in the cyclic program. In the startup projects, the block is called to generate a collective signal for the limit values of the production data. The buttons [ProdData] and [LimitValues] are animated in color, depending on the value range of the limit values.

**Operation mode Automatic / Manual**  

The block is independent of operation modes. Therefor it is not assigned to any operation mode area. </Text>
